	To begin with, developing a good learning habits is able to  help students to improve the learning ability. With a good learning habits, students can be more faster on getting 
new knowledge.  If they have a regular plan, they will know when I should revise the things today learnt and when should I pre- learn the tomorrow lessson.
	Moreover, a good learning habits can protect students' eyes and body.From the recent news, lots of students learnt with a bad figure, which bringed many healthy problems. And 
some students such stayed up late to learn, leading to the bad sleep then they just can sleep at class.
	In conclusion, developing good learning habits is very important for students.


	It is widely acknowledged that good learning habits exert a profound influence on students’ growth. Poor learning habits not only reduce study efficiency but also lead to 
various health troubles among teenagers.
	For one thing, good learning habits greatly improve learning efficiency. Students with proper habits can arrange their study reasonably. They preview lessons in advance and
review knowledge regularly, which helps them absorb knowledge steadily. For another, good learning habits protect students’ physical condition. Correct postures and reasonable 
schedules prevent eye strain and sleep shortage.
	From my perspective, good learning habits are valuable treasures for students. We ought to develop and keep good learning habits to achieve continuous progress.


